 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Rental Application Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a rental application form?\", \"a\": \"A rental application form is what a prospective tenant completes before a landlord offers a lease. It covers rental history and income. It also asks for consent to a credit check. Some landlords call it a tenant application form.\"}, {\"q\": \"How to create a rental application form?\", \"a\": \"List the standards an approval rests on, then turn each into a question. Describe the property and the fee to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>. It builds an online rental application form with a table that holds every applicant.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where can I find a free rental application form in California?\", \"a\": \"Start with your city or county housing department. Before you use any free rental application form, read it against state law. California bars turning away applicants who pay with a housing voucher, and Civil Code 1950.6 requires an itemized receipt for the screening fee. Emergent is free to start, and the free tier covers building and publishing your own version.\"}, {\"q\": \"What does a tenant application form include?\", \"a\": \"A tenant application form asks each adult for their addresses over the past few years, with a phone number for every landlord. Next come the employer and monthly income, backed by recent pay stubs. It closes with the names of everyone moving in and a signed consent to a credit and background check.\"}, {\"q\": \"Which questions should a rent application form leave out?\", \"a\": \"Leave out anything you would not base a decision on. A question about a protected trait, such as birthplace or plans for children, stays off a rent application form even as an optional field. An answer you never used can still look like the reason for a denial.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can an online rental application form collect the screening fee?\", \"a\": \"Yes. An online rental application form can charge the fee as its last step, through the payment account you connect, and email a receipt once it clears. Look up the cap where the unit sits before you pick a number. In New York it is $20, or the real cost of the report when that comes to less.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do landlords review rental application forms?\", \"a\": \"Landlords read them in the order they arrive and hold each one against criteria written down before the listing went up. Income gets confirmed with the employer, and the credit report runs on the consent signed in a tenant screening form. Emergent puts no cap on responses, and a listing that draws 150 applicants keeps taking every one.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where can I find a rental application form in Texas?\", \"a\": \"Landlord associations and property managers in Texas post their own versions, and any of them works if it carries the notice state law asks for. The Property Code says printed notice of your tenant selection criteria must be available when the applicant gets the form. Reject someone without it and you refund the application fee and any deposit.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a rental application form template?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Most templates open with applicant details and rental history, then employment and a signed consent. A rental application form PDF suits a single vacancy, though every paper copy still needs typing into your records. Emergent can also build the form straight from your written criteria, with no template in between.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is a rental application form the same as a lease?\", \"a\": \"No. The application only asks to be considered for the unit, and nothing in it sets the rent or the term. Once you approve someone, those terms go into a lease or a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/rental-agreement-form'>rental agreement form</a> that both sides sign.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
